---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = "How I Work | Mark Gores — Realtor in Prior Lake, MN";
const description = "I'm your main point of contact, start to finish. Responsive, honest, and focused on good decisions over closed deals. 23 years of experience in the south metro.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <h1 class="page-title">How I Work</h1>

    <p class="lead reveal">
      I'm your main point of contact—start to finish. You're not going to get handed off to someone you've never met. When you call, I answer.
    </p>

    <div class="content">
      <section class="section reveal" data-delay="100">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul class="highlights">
          <li><strong>Fast responses.</strong> Usually within an hour during normal hours. Text works best. Evenings and weekends too—real estate doesn't keep office hours.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest opinions.</strong> I'll tell you what I actually think, not what closes the deal. If a house is overpriced, I'll say so. If the timing is wrong, I'll say that too.</li>
          <li><strong>Local knowledge.</strong> I know which neighborhoods flood, which builders cut corners, which streets get highway noise, and which "up and coming areas" have been "up and coming" for 15 years.</li>
          <li><strong>No pressure.</strong> I don't care if you buy this month or next year. I care that when you do buy, you don't regret it.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section reveal" data-delay="150">
        <h2>What actually happens when you call</h2>
        <p>
          I pick up, or I call you back within an hour. We talk about what you're looking for—or what you're trying to sell. I'll ask questions, give you an honest read on the market, and tell you what I'd do if I were in your position.
        </p>
        <p>
          If it makes sense to work together, we do. If it doesn't—if the timing's wrong, or you're better off waiting, or you just need a question answered—that's fine too. No pitch, no follow-up sequence, no "nurturing."
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section reveal" data-delay="200">
        <h2>What I won't do</h2>
        <p>
          I won't add you to a drip campaign. When I reach out, it's because there's something worth saying—not because my CRM told me it's been 90 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          I won't push you to move faster than you're ready. Some agents treat every conversation like it needs to close this quarter. That's not how I operate.
        </p>
        <p>
          I won't do the "just checking in!" calls. If we're working together, you'll hear from me when there's news. If we're not, I'll leave you alone until you're ready.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section reveal" data-delay="250">
        <h2>Good fit</h2>
        <ul class="fit-list">
          <li>You want honest advice, not enthusiastic cheerleading</li>
          <li>You prefer direct communication over scripts and sales pitches</li>
          <li>You're buying or selling in the south metro—Prior Lake, Savage, Shakopee, Lakeville, Burnsville, or nearby</li>
          <li>You value responsiveness and competence over hand-holding</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section reveal" data-delay="300">
        <h2>Not a good fit</h2>
        <ul class="fit-list not-fit">
          <li>You want someone who'll tell you what you want to hear</li>
          <li>You need daily check-ins and constant reassurance</li>
          <li>You're shopping primarily on commission rate</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="fit-note">
          No judgment. Different people need different things. There are plenty of good agents who work differently than I do.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section reveal" data-delay="350">
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>
          I got into real estate in 2003 and spent the first 15 years working alongside my mom at Edina Realty. She'd been in the business for decades and she taught me that this job is about service, not sales. About the relationship you have with someone five years after the closing, not the transaction itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've been through the 2008 crash—I watched the market lose 30% and helped clients navigate short sales and tough decisions. I was there for the COVID frenzy, when people were waiving inspections and offering $50k over asking on houses they'd seen once. And I've worked through every "normal" market in between.
        </p>
        <p>
          That history shapes my advice. I'm not here to convince you that now is always a great time to buy. Sometimes it is. Sometimes it isn't. Sometimes the right move is to wait six months and keep renting. I'll tell you what I honestly think.
        </p>
        <p>
          Now at RE/MAX Advantage Plus. Still in Prior Lake, where I've lived since I was five.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="cta-section reveal" data-delay="400">
        <p>Want to talk through your situation? No commitment, no pitch.</p>
        <div class="cta-buttons">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn">Get in touch</a>
          <a href="/proof" class="btn btn-secondary">Read what clients say</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    max-width: 540px;
  }

  .content {
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .section p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .highlights {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .highlights li {
    padding: var(--space-sm) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    transition: padding-left 0.3s var(--ease-out-expo), background-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .highlights li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .highlights li:hover {
    padding-left: var(--space-sm);
    background-color: var(--color-highlight);
  }

  .highlights strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .fit-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  .fit-list li {
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    transition: padding-left 0.3s var(--ease-out-expo);
  }

  .fit-list li:hover {
    padding-left: calc(var(--space-lg) + var(--space-xs));
  }

  .fit-list li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .fit-list.not-fit li::before {
    content: "—";
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .fit-note {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .cta-section {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .cta-section > p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
</style>
